/target

# Generated coverage + mutation-testing output (ADR-0010 tooling)
/mutants.out
/mutants.out.old
client/coverage
# The lcov the coverage floor and the patch gate are both read from (#22).
/lcov.info
# Seeds proptest saves when a property fails. Upstream recommends committing
# them; this repo deliberately does not. A counterexample worth keeping is worth
# reading, and these are opaque — tens of kilobytes of float arrays naming
# nothing. So a real find gets promoted into the test as a named `rstest` case,
# where the next person can see what it proves, and the seed file stays local.
/proptest-regressions

/rdio-scanner
/sdrtrunk
/radio-scout-data
/radio-scout-live-test
# A/B renders for the enhancement listening test (#36) — real Call audio,
# regenerated by `cargo run --example enhance_ab`.
/enhance-ab

# Local development configuration (secrets). `.env.example` is the template and
# IS committed; the real file never is.
.env

# The configuration file `radio-scout --write-config` writes here (#17). It is
# one operator's local settings — committing one would silently override every
# other developer's defaults. The template lives in the binary (`config::TEMPLATE`),
# so there is nothing to keep a copy of.
/radio-scout.toml

# A root-level npm install (the frontend's own is client/node_modules, which
# client/.gitignore covers).
/node_modules
/trunk-recorder

THEPROJECT.md